1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:02,400
One second he was diving for lobster.

2
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:04,240
The next, everything went black.

3
00:00:04,790 --> 00:00:07,020
Cape Cod, June 2021.

4
00:00:07,270 --> 00:00:10,610
Lobster diver Michael Packard was forty-five feet down.

5
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:11,620
His first thought:

6
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:12,290
a shark.

7
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:13,920
But there were no teeth.

8
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:14,610
No pain.

9
00:00:14,870 --> 00:00:16,440
He was inside a whale's mouth.

10
00:00:16,810 --> 00:00:20,050
Experts think a feeding humpback scooped him up by accident.

11
00:00:20,190 --> 00:00:22,820
He still had his scuba tank, so he kept breathing.

12
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:24,520
He thought he was going to die.

13
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:25,730
He thought of his sons.

14
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:28,670
But a humpback can't actually swallow a person.

15
00:00:28,770 --> 00:00:30,410
Its throat is far too narrow.

16
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:33,610
After thirty to forty seconds, by his own estimate,

17
00:00:33,690 --> 00:00:34,450
he saw light.

18
00:00:34,470 --> 00:00:37,410
The whale surfaced and threw its head side to side,

19
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:38,530
and spat him out.

20
00:00:38,820 --> 00:00:41,810
His crewmate, Josiah Mayo, pulled him from the water.

21
00:00:42,090 --> 00:00:44,180
Bruised, sore, and no broken bones.

22
00:00:44,510 --> 00:00:46,160
A humpback can't swallow you.

23
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:48,670
But it can still close its mouth around you.
